IMPORT `P6-annex-xi-xiii`

-- P6-art-53-54: Chapter V Section 2, Articles 53 and 54, the obligations of providers of general-purpose AI models and their authorised representatives
-- (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744; the consolidated text of 27.7.2026 is a rendering with no legal effect). Neither Article was changed by the Omnibus: one text.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Every function takes `the date asked` first. NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTHING-kind); JUST FALSE is the text's own no (FALSE-kind); JUST TRUE says the rule, duty or power arises.
-- A provider's duty passes the gate `Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` (Chapter V applies from 2 August 2025; Art 111(3) gives a provider of a model placed
-- before then until 2 August 2027). A power of a provider, a duty of an authorised representative and a power of the Commission pass the group only (fork F-111-3-scope).
-- The exceptions for free and open-source models (Article 53(2), Article 54(6)) are computed by their own functions; a duty takes the answer as a BOOLEAN named for it.

DECLARE `Art 53 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 53(1)(a) draw up and keep up-to-date the technical documentation of the model`
    `Art 53(1)(b) draw up, keep up-to-date and make available information and documentation to providers of AI systems who intend to integrate the model into their AI systems`
    `Art 53(1)(c) put in place a policy to comply with Union law on copyright and related rights`
    `Art 53(1)(d) draw up and make publicly available a sufficiently detailed summary about the content used for training of the model`
    `Art 53(3) cooperate as necessary with the Commission and the national competent authorities`
    `Art 53(4) demonstrate alternative adequate means of compliance for assessment by the Commission`

DECLARE `Art 54 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 54(1) appoint, by written mandate, an authorised representative which is established in the Union`
    `Art 54(2) enable the authorised representative to perform the tasks specified in the mandate`
    `Art 54(3) perform the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider`
    `Art 54(3) provide a copy of the mandate to the AI Office`
    `Art 54(5) terminate the mandate`
    `Art 54(5) inform the AI Office about the termination of the mandate and the reasons therefor`

§ `Article 53(2): the exception for free and open-source models`

-- "The obligations set out in paragraph 1, points (a) and (b), shall not apply to providers of AI models that are released under a free and open-source licence that allows for the access, usage,
-- modification, and distribution of the model, and whose parameters, including the weights, the information on the model architecture, and the information on model usage, are made publicly available.
-- This exception shall not apply to general-purpose AI models with systemic risks." The exception applies when all four facts hold and the model is not one with systemic risk.
-- src:794 | 2. The obligations set out in paragraph 1, points (a) and (b), shall not apply to providers of AI models that are released under a free and open-source licence that allows for the access, usage, modification, and distribution of the model, and whose parameters, including the weights, the information on the model architecture, and the information on model usage, are made publicly available. This exception shall not apply to general-purpose AI models with systemic risks.
@ref Art 53(2) (src:794)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model is released under a free and open-source licence that allows for the access, usage, modification, and distribution of the model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parameters of the model, including the weights, are made publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information on the model architecture is made publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information on model usage is made publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 53(2) the exception for free and open-source models applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of the obligations of providers of general-purpose AI models
        IF `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This exception shall not apply to general-purpose AI models with systemic risks"
        OTHERWISE JUST (    `the model is released under a free and open-source licence that allows for the access, usage, modification, and distribution of the model`
                        AND `the parameters of the model, including the weights, are made publicly available`
                        AND `the information on the model architecture is made publicly available`
                        AND `the information on model usage is made publicly available`)
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not apply to providers of AI models that are released under a free and open-source licence ... and whose parameters ... are made publicly available" (the exception is the class the text describes; outside the class it does not apply)

§ `Article 53(1), point (a): the technical documentation`

-- "Providers of general-purpose AI models shall: (a) draw up and keep up-to-date the technical documentation of the model, including its training and testing process and the results of its evaluation, which shall
-- contain, at a minimum, the information set out in Annex XI for the purpose of providing it, upon request, to the AI Office and the national competent authorities". The clause "for the purpose of providing it,
-- upon request" states the purpose of the documentation; it is not read as a separate duty to provide it (fork F-53-1-a-purpose; the other reading: a duty to provide on request, which Article 91 supplies).
-- src:787 | 1. Providers of general-purpose AI models shall:
-- src:788 | (a) draw up and keep up-to-date the technical documentation of the model, including its training and testing process and the results of its evaluation, which shall contain, at a minimum, the information set out in Annex XI for the purpose of providing it, upon request, to the AI Office and the national competent authorities;
@ref Art 53(1)(a) (src:787-788)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for free and open-source models of paragraph 2 applies to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 53(1)(a) the provider must draw up and keep up-to-date the technical documentation of the model` MEANS
    IF `Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives, to a general-purpose AI model, and Art 111(3) can give its provider until 2 August 2027
    ELSE IF `the exception for free and open-source models of paragraph 2 applies to the provider`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The obligations set out in paragraph 1, points (a) and (b), shall not apply to providers of AI models that are released under a free and open-source licence"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:788 | (a) draw up and keep up-to-date the technical documentation of the model, including its training and testing process and the results of its evaluation, which shall contain, at a minimum, the information set out in Annex XI for the purpose of providing it, upon request, to the AI Office and the national competent authorities;
@ref Art 53(1)(a) (what the documentation must be) (src:788)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for free and open-source models of paragraph 2 applies to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has drawn up the technical documentation of the model, including its training and testing process and the results of its evaluation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider keeps the technical documentation up-to-date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains, at a minimum, the information set out in Annex XI` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 53(1)(a) the technical documentation of the model is what the point requires` MEANS
    IF `Art 53(1)(a) the provider must draw up and keep up-to-date the technical documentation of the model` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the exception for free and open-source models of paragraph 2 applies to the provider` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (    `the provider has drawn up the technical documentation of the model, including its training and testing process and the results of its evaluation`
               AND `the provider keeps the technical documentation up-to-date`
               AND `the technical documentation contains, at a minimum, the information set out in Annex XI`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Providers of general-purpose AI models shall: (a) draw up and keep up-to-date the technical documentation ... which shall contain, at a minimum, the information set out in Annex XI" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the point speaks of the provider who is bound by it

@ref Art 53(1)(a) (the duty; no time limit and no consequence in the text)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for free and open-source models of paragraph 2 applies to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 53 act`
`Art 53(1)(a) the provider's duty to draw up and keep up-to-date the technical documentation` MEANS
    IF `Art 53(1)(a) the provider must draw up and keep up-to-date the technical documentation of the model` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the exception for free and open-source models of paragraph 2 applies to the provider` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 53(1)(a) draw up and keep up-to-date the technical documentation of the model`
         -- no time limit and no consequence in the text (listed in NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 53(1), point (b): information and documentation for providers of AI systems`

-- Point (b), with its two sub-points: the information and documentation shall "(i) enable providers of AI systems to have a good understanding of the capabilities and limitations of the general-purpose
-- AI model and to comply with their obligations pursuant to this Regulation; and (ii) contain, at a minimum, the elements set out in Annex XII". "Without prejudice to the need to observe and protect
-- intellectual property rights and confidential business information or trade secrets" adds no element (fork F-53-1-b-without-prejudice).
-- src:789 | (b) draw up, keep up-to-date and make available information and documentation to providers of AI systems who intend to integrate the general-purpose AI model into their AI systems. Without prejudice to the need to observe and protect intellectual property rights and confidential business information or trade secrets in accordance with Union and national law, the information and documentation shall:
-- src:790 | (i) enable providers of AI systems to have a good understanding of the capabilities and limitations of the general-purpose AI model and to comply with their obligations pursuant to this Regulation; and
-- src:791 | (ii) contain, at a minimum, the elements set out in Annex XII;
@ref Art 53(1)(b) (src:789-791)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for free and open-source models of paragraph 2 applies to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 53(1)(b) the provider must draw up, keep up-to-date and make available information and documentation to providers of AI systems` MEANS
    IF `Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives, to a general-purpose AI model, and Art 111(3) can give its provider until 2 August 2027
    ELSE IF `the exception for free and open-source models of paragraph 2 applies to the provider`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The obligations set out in paragraph 1, points (a) and (b), shall not apply to providers of AI models that are released under a free and open-source licence"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:789 | (b) draw up, keep up-to-date and make available information and documentation to providers of AI systems who intend to integrate the general-purpose AI model into their AI systems. Without prejudice to the need to observe and protect intellectual property rights and confidential business information or trade secrets in accordance with Union and national law, the information and documentation shall:
-- src:790 | (i) enable providers of AI systems to have a good understanding of the capabilities and limitations of the general-purpose AI model and to comply with their obligations pursuant to this Regulation; and
-- src:791 | (ii) contain, at a minimum, the elements set out in Annex XII;
@ref Art 53(1)(b) (what the information and documentation must be) (src:789-791)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for free and open-source models of paragraph 2 applies to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has drawn up the information and documentation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider keeps the information and documentation up-to-date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider makes the information and documentation available to providers of AI systems who intend to integrate the model into their AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information and documentation enable providers of AI systems to have a good understanding of the capabilities and limitations of the model and to comply with their obligations pursuant to this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information and documentation contain, at a minimum, the elements set out in Annex XII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 53(1)(b) the information and documentation are what the point requires` MEANS
    IF `Art 53(1)(b) the provider must draw up, keep up-to-date and make available information and documentation to providers of AI systems` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the exception for free and open-source models of paragraph 2 applies to the provider` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (    `the provider has drawn up the information and documentation`
               AND `the provider keeps the information and documentation up-to-date`
               AND `the provider makes the information and documentation available to providers of AI systems who intend to integrate the model into their AI systems`
               AND `the information and documentation enable providers of AI systems to have a good understanding of the capabilities and limitations of the model and to comply with their obligations pursuant to this Regulation`
               AND `the information and documentation contain, at a minimum, the elements set out in Annex XII`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Providers of general-purpose AI models shall: (b) draw up, keep up-to-date and make available information and documentation ... the information and documentation shall: (i) ... (ii) ..." (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the point speaks of the provider who is bound by it

@ref Art 53(1)(b) (the duty; no time limit and no consequence in the text)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for free and open-source models of paragraph 2 applies to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 53 act`
`Art 53(1)(b) the provider's duty to make information and documentation available to providers of AI systems` MEANS
    IF `Art 53(1)(b) the provider must draw up, keep up-to-date and make available information and documentation to providers of AI systems` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the exception for free and open-source models of paragraph 2 applies to the provider` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 53(1)(b) draw up, keep up-to-date and make available information and documentation to providers of AI systems who intend to integrate the model into their AI systems`
         -- no time limit and no consequence in the text (listed in NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 53(1), point (c): the copyright policy`

-- "put in place a policy to comply with Union law on copyright and related rights, and in particular to identify and comply with, including through state-of-the-art technologies, a reservation of rights
-- expressed pursuant to Article 4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790". "In particular" is read as part of what the policy must do (fork F-53-1-c-in-particular; the other reading: emphasis only);
-- "including through state-of-the-art technologies" lists a means without closing the list, so it is no element. The exception of paragraph 2 does not reach point (c).
-- src:792 | (c) put in place a policy to comply with Union law on copyright and related rights, and in particular to identify and comply with, including through state-of-the-art technologies, a reservation of rights expressed pursuant to Article 4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790;
@ref Art 53(1)(c) (src:792)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 53(1)(c) the provider must put in place a policy to comply with Union law on copyright and related rights` MEANS
    IF `Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives, to a general-purpose AI model, and Art 111(3) can give its provider until 2 August 2027
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:792 | (c) put in place a policy to comply with Union law on copyright and related rights, and in particular to identify and comply with, including through state-of-the-art technologies, a reservation of rights expressed pursuant to Article 4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790;
@ref Art 53(1)(c) (what the policy must be) (src:792)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has put in place a policy to comply with Union law on copyright and related rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the policy identifies a reservation of rights expressed pursuant to Article 4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the policy complies with a reservation of rights expressed pursuant to Article 4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 53(1)(c) the copyright policy is what the point requires` MEANS
    IF `Art 53(1)(c) the provider must put in place a policy to comply with Union law on copyright and related rights` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (    `the provider has put in place a policy to comply with Union law on copyright and related rights`
               AND `the policy identifies a reservation of rights expressed pursuant to Article 4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790`
               AND `the policy complies with a reservation of rights expressed pursuant to Article 4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Providers of general-purpose AI models shall: (c) put in place a policy to comply with Union law on copyright and related rights, and in particular to identify and comply with ... a reservation of rights" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the point speaks of the provider who is bound by it

@ref Art 53(1)(c) (the duty; no time limit and no consequence in the text)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 53 act`
`Art 53(1)(c) the provider's duty to put in place a copyright policy` MEANS
    IF `Art 53(1)(c) the provider must put in place a policy to comply with Union law on copyright and related rights` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 53(1)(c) put in place a policy to comply with Union law on copyright and related rights`
         -- no time limit and no consequence in the text (listed in NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 53(1), point (d): the summary of the training content`

