§ `Article 53(3): cooperation`

-- "Providers of general-purpose AI models shall cooperate as necessary with the Commission and the national competent authorities in the exercise of their competences and powers pursuant to this Regulation."
-- "As necessary" is read as a condition of the duty: when cooperation is not necessary for the exercise of their competences and powers the duty does not arise (JUST FALSE; fork F-53-3-as-necessary).
-- src:795 | 3. Providers of general-purpose AI models shall cooperate as necessary with the Commission and the national competent authorities in the exercise of their competences and powers pursuant to this Regulation.
@ref Art 53(3) (src:795)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `cooperation is necessary in the exercise of the competences and powers of the Commission or the national competent authorities pursuant to this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 53(3) the provider must cooperate as necessary with the Commission and the national competent authorities` MEANS
    IF `Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives, to a general-purpose AI model, and Art 111(3) can give its provider until 2 August 2027
    ELSE IF `cooperation is necessary in the exercise of the competences and powers of the Commission or the national competent authorities pursuant to this Regulation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall cooperate as necessary" (a condition: when cooperation is not necessary there is no duty to cooperate)

@ref Art 53(3) (the duty; no time limit and no consequence in the text)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `cooperation is necessary in the exercise of the competences and powers of the Commission or the national competent authorities pursuant to this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 53 act`
`Art 53(3) the provider's duty to cooperate` MEANS
    IF `Art 53(3) the provider must cooperate as necessary with the Commission and the national competent authorities` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `cooperation is necessary in the exercise of the competences and powers of the Commission or the national competent authorities pursuant to this Regulation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 53(3) cooperate as necessary with the Commission and the national competent authorities`
         -- no time limit and no consequence in the text (listed in NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 53(4): codes of practice, harmonised standards, and alternative means`

-- First sentence: "Providers of general-purpose AI models may rely on codes of practice within the meaning of Article 56 to demonstrate compliance with the obligations set out in paragraph 1 of this Article,
-- until a harmonised standard is published." A power of the provider, limited by its own wording to a code within the meaning of Article 56; an "until" bar: JUST TRUE before the publication, JUST FALSE after it
-- (the guide's list of "until" among the words that introduce a condition; fork F-53-4-until: "a harmonised standard" is read as one covering the obligations of paragraph 1, the other reading is any harmonised standard).
-- The power is not delayed by Art 111(3), which delays obligations.
-- src:796 | 4. Providers of general-purpose AI models may rely on codes of practice within the meaning of Article 56 to demonstrate compliance with the obligations set out in paragraph 1 of this Article, until a harmonised standard is published. Compliance with European harmonised standards grants providers the presumption of conformity to the extent that those standards cover those obligations. Providers of general-purpose AI models who do not adhere to an approved code of practice or do not comply with a European harmonised standard shall demonstrate alternative adequate means of compliance for assessment by the Commission.
@ref Art 53(4) first sentence (src:796)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the code of practice is within the meaning of Article 56` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a harmonised standard covering the obligations has been published` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 53(4) the provider may rely on a code of practice to demonstrate compliance with the obligations set out in paragraph 1` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Providers of general-purpose AI models may rely"
        IF NOT `the code of practice is within the meaning of Article 56`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "codes of practice within the meaning of Article 56"
        IF `a harmonised standard covering the obligations has been published`
