§ `Article 54(6): the exception for free and open-source models`

-- "The obligation set out in this Article shall not apply to providers of general-purpose AI models that are released under a free and open-source licence ... unless the general-purpose AI models present
-- systemic risks." "Present systemic risks" is read as: the model is classified as one with systemic risk under Article 51 (fork F-54-6-presents; the other reading: it factually presents a systemic risk).
-- src:811 | 6. The obligation set out in this Article shall not apply to providers of general-purpose AI models that are released under a free and open-source licence that allows for the access, usage, modification, and distribution of the model, and whose parameters, including the weights, the information on the model architecture, and the information on model usage, are made publicly available, unless the general-purpose AI models present systemic risks.
@ref Art 54(6) (src:811)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model is released under a free and open-source licence that allows for the access, usage, modification, and distribution of the model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parameters of the model, including the weights, are made publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information on the model architecture is made publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information on model usage is made publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 54(6) the exception for free and open-source models applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "providers of general-purpose AI models"
        IF `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the general-purpose AI models present systemic risks"
        OTHERWISE JUST (    `the model is released under a free and open-source licence that allows for the access, usage, modification, and distribution of the model`
                        AND `the parameters of the model, including the weights, are made publicly available`
                        AND `the information on the model architecture is made publicly available`
                        AND `the information on model usage is made publicly available`)
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not apply to providers of general-purpose AI models that are released under a free and open-source licence ..." (the exception is the class the text describes; outside the class it does not apply)

