            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives, to a general-purpose AI model, and Art 111(3) can give its provider until 2 August 2027
        IF `the provider's place` EQUALS `Established or located in the Union`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "providers established in third countries"
        IF `the exception for free and open-source models of Article 54(6) applies to the provider`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The obligation set out in this Article shall not apply to providers of general-purpose AI models that are released under a free and open-source licence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- What the appointment must be: before the model is placed on the Union market, by written mandate, of a representative established in the Union. "Prior to" is strict: on the day of the placing is too late.
-- src:802 | 1. Prior to placing a general-purpose AI model on the Union market, providers established in third countries shall, by written mandate, appoint an authorised representative which is established in the Union.
@ref Art 54(1) (what the appointment must be) (src:802)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider's place` IS A `Place of a party`
      `the exception for free and open-source models of Article 54(6) applies to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the authorised representative was appointed` IS A DATE
      `the date the model is placed on the Union market` IS A DATE
      `the appointment is by written mandate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorised representative is established in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 54(1) the appointment of the authorised representative is what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF `Art 54(1) the provider must appoint, by written mandate, an authorised representative which is established in the Union` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the provider's place` `the exception for free and open-source models of Article 54(6) applies to the provider` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (    `the date the authorised representative was appointed` LESS THAN `the date the model is placed on the Union market`
               AND `the appointment is by written mandate`
               AND `the authorised representative is established in the Union`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Prior to placing a general-purpose AI model on the Union market, providers established in third countries shall, by written mandate, appoint an authorised representative which is established in the Union" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of the provider who is bound by it

-- The rule. Day 0 is the date asked. The model is to be placed on the Union market on a later day, and the appointment must be made before that day: the last day for it is the day before.
-- If the model is placed on or before the date asked and no representative has been appointed, the time has run: the rule is breached (the facts say no representative is in place).
@ref Art 54(1) (the duty and its time)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider's place` IS A `Place of a party`
      `the exception for free and open-source models of Article 54(6) applies to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has already appointed an authorised representative by written mandate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the model is placed on the Union market` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 54 act`
`Art 54(1) the provider's duty to appoint an authorised representative` MEANS
    IF `Art 54(1) the provider must appoint, by written mandate, an authorised representative which is established in the Union` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the provider's place` `the exception for free and open-source models of Article 54(6) applies to the provider` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (NOT `the provider has already appointed an authorised representative by written mandate`)
    THEN IF `the date the model is placed on the Union market` GREATER THAN `the date asked`
         THEN PARTY Provider
              MUST `Art 54(1) appoint, by written mandate, an authorised representative which is established in the Union`
              WITHIN (Day `the date the model is placed on the Union market`) MINUS (Day `the date asked`) MINUS 1
              HENCE FULFILLED
              LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "no authorised representative was appointed before the model was placed on the Union market"
         ELSE BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the model is placed on the Union market and no authorised representative was appointed before"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

