§ `Article 54(5): terminating the mandate, and informing the AI Office`

-- "The authorised representative shall terminate the mandate if it considers or has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation."
-- The condition is met by either: that it considers, or that it has reason to consider.
-- src:810 | 5. The authorised representative shall terminate the mandate if it considers or has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation. In such a case, it shall also immediately inform the AI Office about the termination of the mandate and the reasons therefor.
@ref Art 54(5) first sentence (src:810)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorised representative has received a mandate from the provider of the model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for free and open-source models of Article 54(6) applies to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorised representative considers the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorised representative has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 54(5) the authorised representative must terminate the mandate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Article is about authorised representatives of providers of general-purpose AI models
        IF NOT `the authorised representative has received a mandate from the provider of the model`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "terminate the mandate"
        IF `the exception for free and open-source models of Article 54(6) applies to the provider`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The obligation set out in this Article shall not apply to providers of general-purpose AI models that are released under a free and open-source licence"
        IF `the authorised representative considers the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation` OR `the authorised representative has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall terminate the mandate if it considers or has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations" (the "if" is not met)

@ref Art 54(5) first sentence (the duty; no time limit and no consequence in the text)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorised representative has received a mandate from the provider of the model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception for free and open-source models of Article 54(6) applies to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorised representative considers the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorised representative has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 54 act`
`Art 54(5) the authorised representative's duty to terminate the mandate` MEANS
    IF `Art 54(5) the authorised representative must terminate the mandate` `the date asked` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the authorised representative has received a mandate from the provider of the model` `the exception for free and open-source models of Article 54(6) applies to the provider` `the authorised representative considers the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation` `the authorised representative has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `Authorised representative`
         MUST `Art 54(5) terminate the mandate`
         -- no time limit and no consequence in the text (listed in NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

